## Model Task Assignments

Based on `internal/llm/client.go`:

### Fast Model (`LLM_MODEL_FAST`)
- Topic suggestion
- JSON conversion (summary to structured)
- Section extraction
- Encyclopedia source check
- Relevance/redundancy checks
- Improvement scoring
- Search query generation
- New section suggestions

### Article Model (`LLM_MODEL_ARTICLE`)
- Source summarization (plain text, thinking disabled for longer output)
- Entity extraction
- Article generation (with thinking mode)
- Section comparison (with thinking mode)
- Section merging (with thinking mode)
- Content integration (with thinking mode)
- Reference addition

## Pull Models

```bash
ollama pull qwen3:8b
ollama pull deepseek-r1:14b
ollama pull nomic-embed-text
```

## Check Loaded Models

```powershell
# List all models
ollama list

# Check what's currently loaded in memory
Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://localhost:11434/api/ps" | ConvertTo-Json

# Unload a model
ollama stop qwen3:8b
```

## Model Selection Criteria

For article generation, models should:
- Fit fully in GPU VRAM (no CPU offload)
- Support thinking mode for better reasoning
- Produce high word counts (comprehensive extraction)
- Run fast enough for batch processing

## Thinking Mode

Controlled by `LLM_THINK_MODE` environment variable:
- `true` - Enable thinking for supported models (qwen3, deepseek-r1)
- `false` - Disable thinking
- `low`, `medium`, `high` - Thinking intensity for gpt-oss models

Note: Source summarization uses thinking DISABLED even when `LLM_THINK_MODE=true` because it needs longer output (thinking consumes output tokens).

